---
import GuideLayout from "../../layouts/GuideLayout.astro";
import { SCHOOL_PACKAGES, SCHOOL_STUDENT_CAP } from "../../data/school";
import { inr } from "../../data/pricing";
---

<GuideLayout slug="school-management-system-cost-india">
    <p>
        There is no single price for a school management system in India. Cost
        depends on how many modules you need, whether you want store apps,
        messaging and data entry, and how the vendor structures fees. This
        guide explains the line items so you can compare quotes properly. For
        a concrete example we use our own published prices at the end.
    </p>

    <h2>What drives the price</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>Modules.</strong> Attendance and circulars cost less than a
            full suite with fees, exams, report cards, timetable, homework and
            staff leave.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>School size.</strong> Some vendors price by student count,
            others by a size band. Always ask which band your school falls in.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Mobile apps.</strong> An installable web app (PWA) is
            usually cheaper than separate Android and iOS store apps, which
            also need publishing and upkeep.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Website.</strong> A new school website is often a separate
            line item from the management system.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Data setup.</strong> Entering your existing student,
            parent and teacher records is either done by your admin or quoted
            separately.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Languages and customisation.</strong> Hindi or Punjabi
            interfaces, certificates and custom report-card templates are
            usually add-ons.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Two common pricing models</h2>
    <p>
        <strong>One-time build plus yearly maintenance.</strong> You pay for
        development once, then a smaller yearly fee for hosting, updates and
        support. Costs are predictable, and you can see the three-year total
        up front.
    </p>
    <p>
        <strong>Per-student subscription.</strong> A recurring fee per student
        per year. This starts cheap for a small school but grows as admissions
        grow, and you never stop paying for the base system.
    </p>
    <p>
        Neither is always better. Compare the total over three to five years
        for your actual student count.
    </p>

    <h2>Costs that are easy to miss</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>SMS, WhatsApp and OTP messages.</strong> These go through
            third-party providers who charge per message. Ask whether they are
            included or billed at actuals.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Payment gateway charges.</strong> Online fee collection
            through a gateway such as Razorpay carries the gateway's own
            charges, separate from the software price.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Domain renewal.</strong> Typically around ₹1,000 per year,
            paid by the school if the domain is in its name.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Year-two jump.</strong> Check whether the first year of
            hosting and maintenance is included, and what the yearly fee is
            from year two.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Upgrade path.</strong> If you start small, ask what it
            costs to add modules later.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Example: GroverHQ School Management System prices</h2>
    <p>
        These are our published starting prices for schools of up to {SCHOOL_STUDENT_CAP} students. The
        final quote depends on scope. The first year of hosting and maintenance
        is included, and the yearly fee starts from the second year.
    </p>
    <ul>
        {
            SCHOOL_PACKAGES.map((p) => (
                <li>
                    <strong>{p.name}:</strong> from {inr(p.price)} one-time, then {inr(p.amc)} per year from year 2.
                </li>
            ))
        }
    </ul>
    <p>
        Add-ons such as WhatsApp or SMS alerts, OTP login, certificates, Hindi
        or Punjabi interfaces and store apps are priced separately and listed
        on the
        <a href="/services/school-management-system/#add-ons">add-on modules</a>
        section of the School Management System page. Message charges from the
        provider are billed at actuals.
    </p>

    <h2>How to compare quotes</h2>
    <ol>
        <li>List the modules you need and make every vendor quote the same list.</li>
        <li>Ask for the three-year total, including yearly fees.</li>
        <li>Ask what is not included, and who does data entry.</li>
        <li>Ask what happens to your system and data if you stop paying.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
        Our checklist on
        <a href="/guides/how-to-choose-a-school-management-system/">how to choose a school management system</a>
        has the full list of questions to ask.
    </p>
</GuideLayout>
